   "hint": "Phrases against word to word links.",
   "answer": "A constituency parse groups words into nested phrases with labels such as NP and VP, so its nodes are words plus phrase nodes. A dependency parse links each word to its head with a labelled arc such as nsubj or obj, so its nodes are only the words, and a sentence of n words has n arcs including the root. Dependencies suit free word order languages and relation extraction, constituencies suit phrase boundaries and coordination.",
   "explain": "<p>Universal Dependencies provides dependency treebanks for over 100 languages. The Penn Treebank is the classic English constituency treebank.</p>",
